endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 317 0 R
/T (African governments have been struggling to establish frameworks that would measure the impacts of urban climate investments. These investments are known to be multi-dimensional including; physical infrastructure, socio-economic dynamics, and capacity building. Evidence on these multi-dimensional investments on what is working and what is not is critical in informing future climate investment options. Fundamentally, tracking of these investment impacts often reveals whether adaptation capacities of the intended beneficiaries have been enhanced, it exposes the existing disparities and allows for proven interventions to be scaled. )
/E (African governments have been struggling to establish frameworks that would measure the impacts of urban climate investments. These investments are known to be multi-dimensional including; physical infrastructure, socio-economic dynamics, and capacity building. Evidence on these multi-dimensional investments on what is working and what is not is critical in informing future climate investment options. Fundamentally, tracking of these investment impacts often reveals whether adaptation capacities of the intended beneficiaries have been enhanced, it exposes the existing disparities and allows for proven interventions to be scaled. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
